        <h2>Cart recovery workflow test</h2>
        <p>These scenarios and research notes are illustrative proposals, not observed tests. Contribution here means AOV × (gross margin rate − discount rate), with unchanged product cost; the loss is AOV × discount rate, before messaging, shipping, returns and other variable costs. Timings are offsets from abandonment, not a mandatory sequence. Confirm channel availability and permission in the actual integration; a TCPA opt-in label alone does not establish every applicable requirement. Recheck current purchase, stock, consent, quiet hours and suppression state at dispatch, including replayed events.</p>
        <p>$746 cart: email 87m / 16h / SMS 5h. $117 cart: adjust discount cap down 11% max. Exit on purchase; suppress OOS.</p>
        <h2>Channel escalation</h2>
        <p>Email carries proof; SMS compresses urgency; never duplicate paragraphs cross-channel. Cap 3 touches per cart per 7 days.</p>
        <h2>Attribution</h2>
        <p>Propose a randomized 5% holdout; compare contribution per eligible shopper across treatment and holdout over the same window. Platform-attributed orders are not a causal lift estimate; no measured overstatement rate is established here.</p>
